 (the tens place shifted one position to the left): 21 \u00d710=210\n\nAdd them together: 21 +210 =231. Yep, that's correct. So the user's answer of 211 is incorrect. The right answer is 231. I need to explain that clearly.\n\nWait, another way to check: 11 \u00d721. Let's use another method. 11 times 21 is the same as 21 times 11, which is the same as 21 added 11 times. 21+21=42, that's 2 times. 42+21=63 (3), 63+21=84 (4), 84+21=105 (5), 105+21=126 (6), 126+21=147 (7), 147+21=168 (8), 168+21=189 (9), 189+21=210 (10), then add one more 21: 210+21=231. Yep, that's 11 times. So definitely 231. So user made a mistake. The correct answer is 231.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 11 and 21 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n11 \\times 21 = 231\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**  \n1. Break down 21 into \\(20 + 1\\).  \n2. Use the distributive property:  \n   \\[\n   11 \\times (20 + 1) = (11 \\times 20) + (11 \\times 1)\n   \\]  \n3. Calculate each part:  \n   - \\(11 \\times 20 = 220\\)  \n   - \\(11 \\times 1 = 11\\)  \n4. Add the results:  \n   \\[\n   220 + 11 = 231\n   \\]  \n\n**Answer:** The correct product is **231**. The initial guess of 211 is incorrect.",
