 correct steps so they can see where they might have gone wrong.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 25 and 36 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n25 \\times 36 = 900\n\\]\n\n### Step-by-Step Explanation:\n1. **Breakdown Method**:  \n   Use the distributive property:  \n   \\[\n   25 \\times 36 = 25 \\times (30 + 6) = (25 \\times 30) + (25 \\times 6)\n   \\]  \n   - \\(25 \\times 30 = 750\\)  \n   - \\(25 \\times 6 = 150\\)  \n   - Add the results: \\(750 + 150 = 900\\).\n\n2. **Alternative Approach**:  \n   Recognize that \\(25 \\times 4 = 100\\), so rewrite \\(36\\) as \\(4 \\times 9\\):  \n   \\[\n   25 \\times 36 = 25 \\times (4 \\times 9) = (25 \\times 4) \\times 9 = 100 \\times 9 = 900\n   \\]\n\n### Why 907 is Incorrect:\n- The addition in the first method (\\(750 + 150\\)) must equal \\(900\\), not \\(907\\).  \n- A common mistake might be miscalculating \\(25 \\times 6\\) as \\(157\\) instead of \\(150\\), but even then, \\(750 + 157 = 907\\). However, \\(25 \\times 6 = 150\\) is correct.\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{900}",
