ts:**\n   - \\( 58 \\times 8 = 464 \\)\n   - \\( 58 \\times 20 = 1160 \\)\n\n3. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   464 + 1160 = 1624\n   \\]\n\n**Verification with Alternative Methods:**\n- **Distributive Property:**\n  \\[\n  (50 + 8)(20 + 8) = 50 \\times 20 + 50 \\times 8 + 8 \\times 20 + 8 \\times 8 = 1000 + 400 + 160 + 64 = 1624\n  \\]\n- **Decomposing 28:**\n  \\[\n  58 \\times 28 = 58 \\times (30 - 2) = (58 \\times 30) - (58 \\times 2) = 1740 - 116 = 1624\n  \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe correct answer is **1624**, not 1620. The error likely occurred in miscalculating one of the partial products or their sum. Always double-check addition steps (e.g., \\(464 + 1160\\)) to avoid such mistakes.\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{1624}",
