ossible mistake\u2014subtracting 10 somewhere. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they multiplied 84\u00d733 as (80\u00d730) + (4\u00d73) which would be 2400 +12=2412, but that's way off. Probably not. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 84\u00d733 as (85-1)\u00d733 = 85\u00d733 -33. 85\u00d733: 80\u00d733=2640, 5\u00d733=165; total 2640+165=2805. Then subtract 33: 2805-33=2772. Still same. \n\nHmm, so I think the correct answer is 2772, so maybe the user made an error in their initial calculation. Therefore, I should explain the correct steps and point out that the correct answer is 2772, and perhaps where the mistake might have occurred.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 84 and 33 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Calculation:**\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**  \n   \\(84 \\times 33 = 84 \\times (30 + 3)\\)  \n   \\(= (84 \\times 30) + (84 \\times 3)\\)\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**  \n   - \\(84 \\times 30 = 2,\\!520\\)  \n     *(Because \\(84 \\times 3 = 252\\), then \\(252 \\times 10 = 2,\\!520\\))*  \n   - \\(84 \\times 3 = 252\\)  \n\n3. **Add the results:**  \n   \\(2,\\!520 + 252 = 2,\\!772\\)\n\n**Verification via Vertical Multiplication:**  \n```\n    84  \n  \u00d7 33  \n  ------  \n   252   (84 \u00d7 3)  \n+2520    (84 \u00d7 30, shifted one position to the left)  \n  ------  \n  2,772  \n```\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nThe correct answer is **2,772**.  \n\n**Note on the User\u2019s Answer (2,762):**  \nThis result is incorrect. A common mistake here might be miscalculating \\(84 \\times 3\\) as \\(242\\) instead of \\(252\\), leading to \\(2,\\!520 + 242 = 2,\\!762\\). Always double-check intermediate steps to avoid such errors!  \n\nFinal Answer: \\boxed{2772}",
