ard way. Anyway, the correct answer should be 2940. I'll explain that step by step to make sure.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 30 and 98 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property:**  \n   \\( 30 \\times 98 = (3 \\times 10) \\times 98 \\)  \n   \\( = 3 \\times (10 \\times 98) \\)  \n   \\( = 3 \\times 980 \\)  \n   \\( = 2,\\!940 \\).\n\n2. **Alternative method (subtractive approach):**  \n   \\( 98 = 100 - 2 \\), so:  \n   \\( 30 \\times 98 = 30 \\times (100 - 2) \\)  \n   \\( = (30 \\times 100) - (30 \\times 2) \\)  \n   \\( = 3,\\!000 - 60 \\)  \n   \\( = 2,\\!940 \\).\n\nBoth methods confirm that the correct product is **2,940**.  \n\n**Your initial answer of 2,900 is incorrect.** The mistake likely occurred due to an arithmetic error in one of the steps, such as miscalculating \\( 3 \\times 98 \\) or misapplying the distributive property. The correct result is **2,940**.",
