culated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   21 \\times 39 = 21 \\times (40 - 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = (21 \\times 40) - (21 \\times 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 840 - 21 = 819\n   \\]\n\n2. **Alternatively, use the standard algorithm:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n    \\quad 21 \\\\\n   \\times 39 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - Multiply by the **units digit (9):**\n     \\[\n     21 \\times 9 = 189\n     \\]\n   - Multiply by the **tens digit (3, representing 30):**\n     \\[\n     21 \\times 30 = 630\n     \\]\n   - **Add the results:**\n     \\[\n     189 + 630 = 819\n     \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nThe correct product is **819**, not 810. The error likely occurred during addition or a miscalculation in intermediate steps. Always double-check your arithmetic!\n\nANSWER: \\boxed{819}",
