*(6 \u00d7 9 = 54, then add two zeros for the 60 and 90.)*\n\n2. **Second part**:  \n   \\( 60 \\times 2 = 120 \\)\n\n**Adding both results**:  \n\\( 5,\\!400 + 120 = 5,\\!520 \\)\n\n### Final Answer:  \n\\boxed{5520}\n\n---\n\n### Note on the Mistake:  \nThe initial thought of **5,\\!526** is incorrect. The error likely occurred during addition:  \n- \\( 5,\\!400 + 120 = 5,\\!520 \\), not 5,\\!526.  \nDouble-checking each step confirms the correct product is **5,\\!520**.",
