tion error. So the correct answer is 3298.\n\nTherefore, the assistant should explain that the correct product is 3298, not 3498, and show the steps.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 97 and 34 is \\boxed{3298}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 97 and 34, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\n1. Calculate \\( 97 \\times 30 \\):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 30 = 97 \\times (3 \\times 10) = (97 \\times 3) \\times 10 = 291 \\times 10 = 2910\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 97 \\times 4 \\):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 4 = (90 \\times 4) + (7 \\times 4) = 360 + 28 = 388\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two calculations:\n   \\[\n   2910 + 388 = 2910 + 300 + 88 = 3210 + 88 = 3298\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 97 and 34 is \\(\\boxed{3298}\\).",
