\times 48 = 50 \\times 48 - 1 \\times 48 = 2400 - 48 = 2352\n\\]\n\n**Method 3: Difference of Squares (Alternative Approach)**  \n\\[\n49 \\times 48 = (50 - 1)(50 - 2) = 50^2 - 50 \\times 3 + 2 = 2500 - 150 + 2 = 2352\n\\]\n\n**Conclusion**  \nThe correct answer is **2352**.  \n\n**Note on the User's Answer (2392):**  \nA common mistake is miscalculating \\(50 \\times 48 - 1 \\times 48\\). If you accidentally subtract only \\(8\\) (instead of \\(48\\)), you get \\(2400 - 8 = 2392\\). Always ensure you subtract the full product of the subtracted term (e.g., \\(1 \\times 48 = 48\\)).  \n\nFinal Answer: \\boxed{2352}",
