ct, and the correct product is 792. I should explain that so they can see where the mistake happened.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 36 and 22 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down using distributive property**:  \n   \\( 36 \\times 22 = 36 \\times (20 + 2) \\)  \n   \\( = (36 \\times 20) + (36 \\times 2) \\)\n\n2. **Calculate each part**:  \n   - \\( 36 \\times 20 = 720 \\) (since \\(36 \\times 2 = 72\\), then add a zero)  \n   - \\( 36 \\times 2 = 72 \\)\n\n3. **Add the results**:  \n   \\( 720 + 72 = 792 \\)\n\n**Verification via standard multiplication**:  \n```\n   36  \n\u00d7 22  \n------  \n   72   (36 \u00d7 2)  \n+720   (36 \u00d7 20, shifted left)  \n------  \n  792  \n```\n\n**Conclusion**:  \nThe correct answer is **792**, not 892. The discrepancy likely arose from an addition error. Always double-check your calculations using different methods to confirm accuracy!\n\n<\uff5cAnswer\uff5c>  \nThe product of 36 and 22 is \\boxed{792}.",
