ng them together as 3550 + 426: 3550 + 400 is 3950, plus 26 is 3976. So, yeah, I think that's correct. The user must have made an arithmetic error. Therefore, the correct product is 3976.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 71 and 56 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using standard multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 71 by 6 (units place of 56):\n     \\[\n     71 \\times 6 = 426\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 71 by 50 (tens place of 56):\n     \\[\n     71 \\times 50 = 3550\n     \\]\n   - Add the two results:\n     \\[\n     426 + 3550 = \\mathbf{3976}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Verification using distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   (70 + 1)(50 + 6) = 70 \\times 50 + 70 \\times 6 + 1 \\times 50 + 1 \\times 6 = 3500 + 420 + 50 + 6 = \\mathbf{3976}\n   \\]\n\n**Conclusion:** The correct product of 71 and 56 is **3976**. The initial thought of 3676 is incorrect due to a miscalculation during addition. \n\n\\boxed{3976}",
