 = 50 \\times 80 + 50 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 80 + 3 \\times 1 \\)  \n   \\( = 4000 + 50 + 240 + 3 \\)  \n   \\( = 4293 \\).\n\n2. **Verification via standard multiplication**:  \n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   \\quad &\\ \\ 53 \\\\\n   \\times &\\ \\ 81 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\quad &\\ \\ 53 \\quad (\\text{53 \u00d7 1}) \\\\\n   + &4240 \\quad (\\text{53 \u00d7 80, shifted left by 1}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\quad &4293\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer**:  \n\\boxed{4293}  \n\nThe initial guess of \"0293\" is incorrect due to a miscalculation. The correct result is **4293**.",
