n.  \n\\[\n80 \\times 98 = 80 \\times (100 - 2)\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Apply the distributive property:  \n\\[\n80 \\times 100 - 80 \\times 2\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Compute each term:  \n\\[\n8,\\!000 - 160 = 7,\\!840\n\\]\n\n**Verification:** Multiply directly using the standard algorithm:  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad \\ 98 \\\\\n\\times \\,80 \\\\\n\\hline\n7,\\!840 \\quad (\\text{since } 98 \\times 80 = 98 \\times 8 \\times 10)\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{7840}\n\\]\n\nThe initial thought of 7849 is incorrect. The correct product is **7,840**.",
