- b) = 100 - 9 - 2 = 89\n   \\]\n3. **Calculate the second part (product of the differences):**\n   \\[\n   a \\times b = 9 \\times 2 = 18\n   \\]\n4. **Combine both parts:**\n   \\[\n   89 \\quad \\text{(first part)} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 18 \\quad \\text{(second part)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 8918\n   \\]\n\n---\n\n### **Method 2: Standard Multiplication**\n\\[\n91 \\times 98 = 91 \\times (100 - 2) = 91 \\times 100 - 91 \\times 2 = 9100 - 182 = 8918\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### **Why the Answer Isn\u2019t 8912**\n- If you miscalculate \\(9 \\times 2\\) as \\(12\\) instead of \\(18\\), you might get \\(8912\\), but this is incorrect. Always ensure the product of the differences (\\(a \\times b\\)) matches correctly.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{8918}",
