 just write that out clearly.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 21 and 41 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n21 \\times 41 = (20 + 1) \\times (40 + 1)\n\\]\n\nUsing the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\\[\n= 20 \\times 40 + 20 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 40 + 1 \\times 1 \\\\\n= 800 + 20 + 40 + 1 \\\\\n= 861\n\\]\n\nAlternatively, breaking it down step-by-step:\n\\[\n21 \\times 40 = 840 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 21 \\times 1 = 21 \\\\\n\\text{Adding these:} \\quad 840 + 21 = 861\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{861}\n\n**Note:** The initial thought of 860 might arise from an error in adding (e.g., miscalculating \\(840 + 20\\) instead of \\(840 + 21\\)), but the correct result is **861**.",
