ion:**  \nThe correct answer is **1120**, not 5120. The confusion might arise from an arithmetic error during calculation. Always break down the problem or use verification steps to ensure accuracy.\n\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>  \nThe product of 56 and 20 is **1120**.  \n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**  \n1. **Break down 20** into \\( 2 \\times 10 \\):  \n   \\[\n   56 \\times 20 = 56 \\times (2 \\times 10)\n   \\]  \n2. **Multiply 56 by 2**:  \n   \\[\n   56 \\times 2 = 112\n   \\]  \n3. **Multiply the result by 10**:  \n   \\[\n   112 \\times 10 = 1120\n   \\]  \n\n**Verification:**  \nUsing the standard multiplication algorithm:  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   56 \\\\\n\\times 20 \\\\\n\\hline\n   00 \\quad (\\text{56 \u00d7 0}) \\\\\n+1120 \\quad (\\text{56 \u00d7 20, shifted left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  1120 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]  \n\nThe correct answer is **1120**. The initial thought of 5120 likely contains an arithmetic error. Always double-check using different methods!",
