messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 27 and 31?. I think the correct answer is: 836\n', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 27 and 31. Hmm, let me think about how to do this. Multiplying two numbers.. I remember that multiplication is basically repeated addition, but adding 27 thirty-one times would take forever. There must be a faster way.\n\nWait, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me recall how that works. You line up the numbers vertically, right? Let me write them down:.\n\n\u2003\xa027.\n×\xa031.\n------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit of the bottom number, which is 1 in the ones place. Multiply that by 27. So 1 times 27 is 27. Then, move to the next digit, which is 3 in the tens place. Since it's the tens place, I need to remember to shift one position to the left. So 3 times 27. Let me calculate that. 3 times 7 is 21, and 3 times 20 is 60, so 60 + 21 is 81. But since it's the tens place, it's actually 30 times 27, so maybe I should think of it as 30 × 27. Wait, maybe I confused myself there.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking it down using distributive property would help. Like, 27 × 31 is the same as 27 × (30 + 1) which equals 27×30 + 27×1. That seems right. Let me compute each part separately.\n\nFirst, 27 × 30. Hmm, 27 times 10 is 270, so times 3 would be 810. So 27×30 = 810. Then 27×1 is just 27. Adding those together: 810 + 27. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
