messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 22 and 33?. I think the correct answer is: 727\n', '<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 22 and 33. Let me think about how to do this. Multiplication, right? So 22 times 33. Hmm, maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. .\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying numbers can sometimes be simplified by using the distributive property. Like, 22 times 33 is the same as 22 multiplied by (30 + 3). Let me try that. So, 22 times 30 plus 22 times 3. .\n\nCalculating 22 times 30.. Well, 22 times 10 is 220, so 22 times 30 would be three times that, which is 660. Then 22 times 3 is 66. Adding those together: 660 + 66. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
