imes 20 + 2 \\times 20 = 200 + 40 = 240 \\).\n\n### Why 340 is Incorrect:\n- A common mistake might involve adding instead of multiplying (\\(20 + 12 = 32\\)), but this is unrelated to the question.  \n- Alternatively, miscalculating \\(20 \\times 17\\) (which equals 340) could lead to confusion, but the problem specifies \\(20 \\times 12\\).\n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{240}\\).",
