ke. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps they multiplied 89 \u00d7 33 as (90 \u00d7 33) - (1\u00d733) = 2970 - 33 = 2937. So yeah, definitely 2937. \n\nTherefore, the user's answer of 2137 is incorrect. The correct product is 2937.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 89 and 33 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property**:\n   - \\( 89 \\times 30 = 2670 \\)  \n   - \\( 89 \\times 3 = 267 \\)  \n   - **Sum**: \\( 2670 + 267 = 2937 \\).\n\n2. **Verification using alternative method**:\n   - \\( (90 - 1) \\times 33 = 90 \\times 33 - 1 \\times 33 = 2970 - 33 = 2937 \\).\n\n**Final Answer**:  \n\\boxed{2937}  \n\n*Note: The initial guess of 2137 is incorrect due to a miscalculation. The correct result is 2937.*",
