 out the discrepancy.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 50 and 73 is calculated as follows:  \n\\[\n50 \\times 73 = 50 \\times (70 + 3) = (50 \\times 70) + (50 \\times 3)\n\\]\nBreaking it down:  \n- \\(50 \\times 70 = 3,\\!500\\)  \n- \\(50 \\times 3 = 150\\)  \n\nAdding the results:  \n\\[\n3,\\!500 + 150 = 3,\\!650\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{3650}\\)  \n\n*Note: The initial thought of 3,610 may stem from an arithmetic error. Always verify by breaking down the multiplication step by step.*",
