ely, maybe they did 55\u00d788 as 55\u00d7(90 - 2). Wait, 55\u00d790 is 4,950, minus 55\u00d72 is 110. So 4,950 - 110 is 4,840. \n\nHmm. So unless they added 55\u00d788 as 55\u00d780 (4,400) plus 55\u00d78 (440) and then added an extra 9, perhaps mistyping the numbers. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they thought 55\u00d788 as (50\u00d780)+(5\u00d78) which is 4,000 + 40 = 4,040, but that's way off. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 55\u00d78\u00d711, but miscalculated 55\u00d78 as 450 instead of 440, so 450\u00d711 is 4,950. Then subtracted something? Not sure. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 55\u00d788 as (55\u00d7 (80 + 8)) and thought 55\u00d780 is 4,400, then 55\u00d78 as 440, but added them as 4,400 + 440 = 4,840, but then maybe added another 9 because they thought they missed a step? \n\nAlternatively, maybe they thought of 55+88 first, but that's 143, then multiplied by 34 or something? Doesn't make sense. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they used a calculator but entered wrong numbers. Like, 55\u00d789 instead of 55\u00d788? 55\u00d789 is 4,895. Hmm, not 4,849. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they pressed 55\u00d789 by mistake, but that's 4,895. Still not 4,849. \n\nAlternatively, 55\u00d788 is 4,840, but maybe they thought of 55\u00d789 as 55\u00d790 minus 55, which is 4,950 - 55 = 4,895. Not helpful. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they added 55+88=143 and then multiplied by 34? 143\u00d734=4,862. Not 4,849 either. \n\nHmm. Alternatively, maybe they multiplied 55\u00d788 as (50\u00d780)+(5\u00d78) + (50\u00d78)+(5\u00d780). Wait, that's the expansion. \n\nWait, (a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd. So 50\u00d780 is 4,000. 50\u00d78 is 400. 5\u00d780 is 400. 5\u00d78 is 40. So total is 4,000+400+400+40=4,840. \n\nSo all methods give 4,840, but the user says 4,849. So 4,840 vs 4,849. The difference is 9. So perhaps they added an extra 9 somewhere. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they multiplied 55\u00d788 as (55\u00d7 (100 - 12)) = 55\u00d7100 -55\u00d712. Let's see, that's 5,500 - 660 = 4,840. \