 answer is 6700. I should present that clearly.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 100 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together. Here's the step-by-step solution:\n\n1. **Understanding Multiplication by 100**:  \n   Multiplying any number by 100 appends two zeros to the end of that number.  \n   For example:  \n   \\( 5 \\times 100 = 500 \\quad \\text{(add two zeros to 5)} \\),  \n   \\( 12 \\times 100 = 1200 \\quad \\text{(add two zeros to 12)} \\).\n\n2. **Applying to 67**:  \n   \\( 67 \\times 100 = 67{,\\!}00 \\).  \n\n3. **Verification**:  \n   - Break down \\( 100 \\) into \\( 10 \\times 10 \\):  \n     \\( 67 \\times 10 = 670 \\),  \n     \\( 670 \\times 10 = 6{,}700 \\).  \n   - Alternatively, use the distributive property:  \n     \\( (60 + 7) \\times 100 = 60 \\times 100 + 7 \\times 100 = 6{,}000 + 700 = 6{,}700 \\).\n\n**Final Answer**:  \nThe product of 67 and 100 is \\(\\boxed{6700}\\).  \n\nYour initial thought of \\(6300\\) was incorrect, but this is the correct solution!",
