messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 51 and 73?. I think the correct answer is: 3223\n', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 51 and 73. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. I remember multiplication is basically repeated addition, but adding 51 seventy-three times would take forever. There has to be a smarter way.\n\nMaybe I can break down the numbers into smaller parts. Let me recall the distributive property: a × (b + c) = a×b + a×c. That might help here. Let's see, 73 can be split into 70 + 3. So, 51 times 73 is the same as 51 times (70 + 3). Applying the distributive property, that becomes (51×70) + (51×3). .\n\nAlright, let me compute each part separately. Starting with 51×70. Hmm, 51 times 70. Well, 51 times 7 is easier. 50×7 is 350, and 1×7 is 7, so 350 +7 = 357. But since it's 70 instead of 7, I need to multiply by 10. So 357×10 = 3570. Okay, so 51×70 is 3570.\n\nNow the second part: 51×3. That's straightforward. 50×3 is 150, and 1×3 is 3, so 150 +3 = 153. .\n\nAdding both results together: 3570 + 153. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
