ther.\n\nWait, but actually, when you do 43 × 70, you can write it as 3010? Let me check that. Because 43 × 7 is 301, so 43 × 70 is 301 ×10, which is 3010. So then adding 86 and 3010.\n\nSo 3010 + 86. Let me compute that. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
