rect. I should explain that the correct answer is 2610 and point out where they might have gone wrong.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 90 and 29 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n90 \\times 29 = 90 \\times (30 - 1) = (90 \\times 30) - (90 \\times 1) = 2700 - 90 = \\boxed{2610}\n\\]\n\n**Explanation:**  \n- Breaking down \\(29\\) as \\(30 - 1\\) simplifies the multiplication.  \n- First, compute \\(90 \\times 30 = 2700\\).  \n- Subtract \\(90 \\times 1 = 90\\) from \\(2700\\):  \n\\[\n2700 - 90 = 2610\n\\]\n\nThe correct answer is **2610**, not 2710. Double-checking with alternative methods (e.g., \\(90 \\times 20 + 90 \\times 9 = 1800 + 810 = 2610\\)) confirms this result. The discrepancy likely arose from an arithmetic error during manual calculation.",
