alculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   45 \\times 92 = 45 \\times (90 + 2) = (45 \\times 90) + (45 \\times 2)\n   \\]\n   - \\(45 \\times 90 = 4050\\)\n   - \\(45 \\times 2 = 90\\)\n\n2. **Sum the results**:\n   \\[\n   4050 + 90 = 4140\n   \\]\n\n3. **Verification via vertical multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 45 by 2 (units place):  \n     \\(45 \\times 2 = 90\\)\n   - Multiply 45 by 90 (tens place, shifted left by one digit):  \n     \\(45 \\times 90 = 4050\\)\n   - Add the partial products:  \n     \\(90 + 4050 = 4140\\)\n\n**Final Answer**:  \nThe product of 45 and 92 is \\(\\boxed{4140}\\).",
