parately:\n   - \\(60 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     60 \\times 75 = 60 \\times (70 + 5) = 60 \\times 70 + 60 \\times 5 = 4200 + 300 = 4500\n     \\]\n   - \\(1 \\times 75 = 75\\)\n\n4. Subtract the results:\n   \\[\n   4500 - 75 = 4425\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication method:\n1. Multiply 59 by 5 (units place of 75):\n   \\[\n   59 \\times 5 = 295\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 59 by 70 (tens place of 75):\n   \\[\n   59 \\times 70 = 59 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 413 \\times 10 = 4130\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results:\n   \\[\n   295 + 4130 = 4425\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 59 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{4425}\\). The initial thought of 5425 is incorrect.",
