imes 79 = (90 + 5)(70 + 9) = 90 \\times 70 + 90 \\times 9 + 5 \\times 70 + 5 \\times 9 = 6,\\!300 + 810 + 350 + 45 = 7,\\!505\n  \\]\n\n- **Adjustment from a round number**:  \n  \\[\n  95 \\times 79 = 95 \\times (80 - 1) = (95 \\times 80) - 95 = 7,\\!600 - 95 = 7,\\!505\n  \\]\n\n**Conclusion**:  \nThe correct product of 95 and 79 is **7,505**. The initial answer of 7,555 is incorrect, likely due to an arithmetic error during addition or miscalculation of one of the intermediate steps. Always double-check by using different methods to ensure accuracy!\n\n<\uff5cFinal Answer\uff5c> The product of 95 and 79 is \\boxed{7505}.",
