messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 28 and 79?. I think the correct answer is: 0212\n', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 28 and 79. Hmm, let me think. Multiplying two numbers can sometimes be tricky, especially if they're not too small. Let me recall how multiplication works. The product of two numbers is basically adding one number to itself as many times as the other number says. But doing that manually here would take too long. Maybe I should use the standard multiplication algorithm?.\n\nAlright, let me write it down step by step. Let's see, 28 times 79. I can write this as 28 × 79. Now, in the standard method, you break it down into parts. Since 79 is 70 + 9, maybe I can do 28 times 70 plus 28 times 9. That should work because of the distributive property, right?.\n\nFirst, let's compute 28 × 70. Hmm, 28 times 7 is 196, so if I multiply that by 10, it becomes 1960. Wait, no, actually 28 × 70 is the same as 28 × 7 × 10. Let me check that again. 28 × 7 is indeed 196, so 196 × 10 is 1960. Okay, that part seems right.\n\nNow, the other part is 28 × 9. Let me calculate that. 28 times 9.. 28 × 10 is 280, so subtracting 28 gives 280 - 28 = 252. So 28 × 9 is 252. .\n\nNow, adding those two results together: 1960 + 252. Let me add them. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
