0 -96 = 7104. Again, same answer. So, definitely 7104.\n\nTherefore, the user's answer of 7304 is incorrect. Probably a miscalculation when adding. Let me see where they might have gone wrong. If they added 6300 + 420 + 360 +24, perhaps they added 6300 + 420 as 6720, then 6720 + 360 might have been miscalculated as 7080, but that's correct. Then 7080 +24 is 7104. Hmm, maybe they thought 70*90 is 7300? But 70*90 is 6300. So maybe they did 70*90 as 70*9*10, which is 630, but then multiplied by 10 again? Wait, no, that would be 6300. Hmm. Alternatively, maybe they thought 74*96 as (70+4)*(90+6), but added wrong. Maybe they added 70*90 and 4*6 first, then the cross terms wrong. Alternatively, perhaps the user added 6300 + 420 as 6720, then added 360 to get 7080, then added 24 and for some reason added an extra 200? Maybe they thought 7080 + 24 is 7104 but wrote 7304 by mistake. \n\nIn any case, according to all the methods I used, the correct product is 7104. So the user's thought answer of 7304 is incorrect. Therefore, I should explain the correct process and point out where the mistake might have occurred.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 74 and 96 is calculated as follows:\n\n### Method 1: Distributive Property\nBreak down the numbers:\n\\[\n(70 + 4) \\times (90 + 6) = 70 \\times 90 + 70 \\times 6 + 4 \\times 90 + 4 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n70 \\times 90 &= 6,\\!300, \\\\\n70 \\times 6 &= 420, \\\\\n4 \\times 90 &= 360, \\\\\n4 \\times 6 &= 24.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdd the results:\n\\[\n6,\\!300 + 420 + 360 + 24 = 7,\\!104.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Standard Multiplication\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad 74 \\\\\n\\times 96 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 444 \\quad (\\text{74} \\times 6) \\\\\n+6,\\!660 \\quad (\\text{74} \\times 90) \\\\\n\\hline\n7,\\!104 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Method 3: Difference of Squares (Alternative Approach)\nRewrite \\(96\\) as \\(100 - 4\\):\n\\[\n74 \\times 96 = 74 \\times (100 - 4) = 74 \\times 100 - 74 \\times 4 = 7,\\!400 - 296 = 7,\\!104.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion\nThe correct answer is **7,104**. The initial guess of **7,304** is incorrect, likely due to an addition error during the calculation. Always double-check each step to avoid mistakes!\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7104}\n\\]",
