ncorrect, likely due to an arithmetic error during calculation.\n\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>The product of 80 and 23 is calculated as follows:  \n1. Break down using the distributive property:  \n   \\( 80 \\times 20 = 1600 \\)  \n   \\( 80 \\times 3 = 240 \\)  \n2. Add the results:  \n   \\( 1600 + 240 = 1840 \\).  \n\n**Verification**:  \n- Standard multiplication confirms \\( 80 \\times 23 = 1840 \\).  \n- Alternative method: \\( (23 \\times 8) \\times 10 = 184 \\times 10 = 1840 \\).  \n\n**Final Answer**: \\(\\boxed{1840}\\).",
