  \n\\[\n18 \\times 42 = 18 \\times (40 + 2) = (18 \\times 40) + (18 \\times 2)\n\\]  \n\nCalculate each part separately:  \n1. \\( 18 \\times 40 = 720 \\)  \n   - \\( 18 \\times 4 = 72 \\), then append a zero: \\( 72 \\times 10 = 720 \\).  \n2. \\( 18 \\times 2 = 36 \\)  \n\nAdd the results together:  \n\\[\n720 + 36 = 756\n\\]  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{756}  \n\nYour initial guess of 746 is incorrect. The correct calculation confirms the product is **756**.",
