      "text": "7347.\n\nWait a second, but the user said they thought the correct answer was 1347. That seems way too small. Let me check my calculations again. Maybe I made an error in the partial products or the addition.\n\nFirst partial product: 93\u00d79. Let me recalculate that. 9\u00d73 is 27, so 7 with 2 carried over. 9\u00d79 is 81 plus 2 is 83. So 837. That seems right.\n\nSecond partial product: 93\u00d770. Since 7 is in the tens place, so it's 70. 93\u00d770. Let's compute 93\u00d77 first. 7\u00d73 is 21, write 1 carry 2. 7\u00d79 is 63 plus 2 is 65. So 651. Then adding a zero at the end gives 6510. That's correct.\n\nAdding 837 + 6510: Let's do this again. 837 + 6510. 800 + 6500 = 7300. Then 37 + 10 = 47, so total is 7347. Hmm. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I should use another method to verify. Let's try the distributive property. 93\u00d779. Break it down into (90 + 3)(70 + 9). \n\nMultiply each term:\n\nFirst, 90\u00d770 = 6300.\n\nThen, 90\u00d79 = 810.\n\nNext, 3\u00d770 = 210.\n\nFinally, 3\u00d79 = 27.\n\nAdd all those together: 6300 + 810 = 7110; 7110 + 210 = 7320; 7320 + 27 = 7347. \n\nSame result. So maybe the user's answer of 1347 is incorrect. Let me compute 93\u00d779 on a calculator. Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but maybe I can compute it another way. Let's see.\n\nAlternatively, 93\u00d780 would be 93\u00d78\u00d710. 93\u00d78 = 744. So 744\u00d710 = 7440. Then subtract 93 to get 93\u00d779: 7440 - 93 = 7347. Yep, that matches. \n\nSo the correct answer is 7347, not 1347. Maybe the user made a mistake in their calculation. Let me see where they might have gone wrong. If they did 9\u00d77 = 63, then 3\u00d79 = 27, added them together 63 +27 = 90, but that's not how multiplication works. Alternatively, maybe they multiplied 90\u00d770 =6300, 3\u00d79=27, added those? 6300+27 is 6327, which is still not 1347. Hmm. Alternatively, maybe they did 9\u00d77 =63, wrote that, then 3\u00d79=27, then added 63+27=90, then thought that's the answer