  ------\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply 93 by 9 (ones place of 79):**\n   - \\( 3 \\times 9 = 27 \\) \u2192 Write down 7, carry over 2.\n   - \\( 9 \\times 9 = 81 + 2 = 83 \\).\n   - **Partial Product:** 837\n\n3. **Multiply 93 by 70 (tens place of 79, shifted left by one digit):**\n   - \\( 3 \\times 7 = 21 \\) \u2192 Write down 1, carry over 2.\n   - \\( 9 \\times 7 = 63 + 2 = 65 \\).\n   - **Partial Product:** 6510 (shifted left: 6510).\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**\n   ```\n     837\n   +6510\n   ------\n    7347\n   ```\n\n**Verification via Distributive Property:**\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n93 \\times 79 &= (90 + 3)(70 + 9) \\\\\n&= 90 \\times 70 + 90 \\times 9 + 3 \\times 70 + 3 \\times 9 \\\\\n&= 6300 + 810 + 210 + 27 \\\\\n&= 6300 + 810 = 7110 \\\\\n&= 7110 + 210 = 7320 \\\\\n&= 7320 + 27 = \\boxed{7347}.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nThe correct product of 93 and 79 is **7,347**, not 1,347. The discrepancy likely arose from an error in partial product calculation or addition. Always double-check using alternative methods!",
