ty:\n\n\\[\n41 \\times 42 = 41 \\times (40 + 2) = (41 \\times 40) + (41 \\times 2)\n\\]\n\n1. **Calculate \\(41 \\times 40\\):**\n   \\[\n   41 \\times 40 = 41 \\times (4 \\times 10) = (41 \\times 4) \\times 10 = 164 \\times 10 = 1640\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(41 \\times 2\\):**\n   \\[\n   41 \\times 2 = 82\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the results:**\n   \\[\n   1640 + 82 = 1722\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{1722}\\)\n\nThe user's proposed answer \"0722\" is incorrect. The correct product of 41 and 42 is **1722**.",
