 can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers:\n\n1. Break down 44 into 40 and 4:\n   \\[\n   (40 + 4) \\times 75\n   \\]\n2. Distribute the multiplication over addition:\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 75 + 4 \\times 75\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each part separately:\n   - For \\(40 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     40 \\times 75 = 40 \\times (70 + 5) = 40 \\times 70 + 40 \\times 5 = 2800 + 200 = 3000\n     \\]\n   - For \\(4 \\times 75\\):\n     \\[\n     4 \\times 75 = 4 \\times (70 + 5) = 4 \\times 70 + 4 \\times 5 = 280 + 20 = 300\n     \\]\n4. Add the results of the two parts:\n   \\[\n   3000 + 300 = 3300\n   \\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 44 by 5: \\(44 \\times 5 = 220\\)\n- Multiply 44 by 70 (since 7 is in the tens place): \\(44 \\times 70 = 3080\\)\n- Add the results: \\(220 + 3080 = 3300\\)\n\nAnother method using the fact that 75 is \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of 100:\n- Calculate \\(44 \\times \\frac{3}{4} = 33\\)\n- Multiply by 100: \\(33 \\times 100 = 3300\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 44 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{3300}\\).",
