200 + 420 = 4620 \\\\\n   4620 + 540 = 5160 \\\\\n   5160 + 54 = \\boxed{5214}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Alternative method (simpler):**\n   \\[\n   79 \\times 66 = (80 - 1) \\times 66 \\\\\n   = 80 \\times 66 - 1 \\times 66 \\\\\n   = 5280 - 66 \\\\\n   = \\boxed{5214}\n   \\]\n\n**Verification:**\n- Multiplying directly:\n  \\[\n  79 \\times 66 = 79 \\times (60 + 6) = 4740 + 474 = 5214\n  \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nThe correct answer is **5214**, not 5514. The initial thought of 5514 likely resulted from an arithmetic error during addition or multiplication.\n\n<\uff5cAnswer\uff5c>  \nThe product of 79 and 66 is **\\boxed{5214}.**  \n<\uff5cConfidence\uff5c>  \nThe correct answer is definitively **5214**, as verified by multiple methods. The user\u2019s proposed answer (5514) is incorrect.  \n<\uff5cExplanation\uff5c>  \nCommon mistakes include misaligning digits during multiplication or miscalculating partial sums. The breakdown above ensures accuracy by systematically addressing each component of the problem.",
